    {
      "id": "draft_issue_spec",
      "kind": "llm_prompt",
      "title": "Draft issue spec",
      "dotAttributes": {
        "class": "issue_writer",
        "benchmark_job_id": "goal.write_issue.write",
        "llm_path_id": "capability.write_issue_item.draft_issue_spec",
        "prompt_version": "2026-03-09.r1",
        "role_version": "1.0.0",
        "skill_id": "goal.write_issue",
        "llm_model": "openai/gpt-5.3-codex",
        "label": "Draft issue spec",
        "output_key": "issue_spec_raw",
        "output_format": "json",
        "reasoning_effort": "medium",
        "timeout": "${goal_decomposition_timeouts.issue_draft}",
        "prompt": "Use read to load ${capability_goal_decomposition_skills}/issue_writer/current.md and follow its guidance on issue structure.\n\nYou are drafting a single implementation issue spec for GitHub.\n\nIntent stack JSON:\n${intent_stack}\n\nGoal issue JSON:\n${goal_issue}\n\nGoal context JSON:\n${goal_context}\n\nFeature JSON:\n${feature}\n\nReviewer notes (if any):\n${review_notes}\n\nDownstream execution constraints:\n- This issue will be executed by one coding agent and reviewed by one semantic reviewer on a shared wave branch.\n- The issue must be implementable as a single implementation issue, not a coordination umbrella or a meta-task.\n- The reviewer will judge whether the implementation satisfies the issue and remains aligned to the parent goal.\n- The issue body must give the builder enough context to start immediately without first rediscovering the codebase.\n- Include specific file paths, functions, tests, and boundaries whenever goal_context supports them.\n- Acceptance criteria must be concrete, observable, and scoped to what this one issue can complete.\n\nBefore drafting, sanity-check the feature itself:\n- If the feature mainly describes scaffolding, fallback continuity, decomposition support, or meta-work instead of a real shipped increment, do not simply polish it into a nicer issue.\n- Rewrite the issue so it directly ships one meaningful slice of the parent goal's promised product surface.\n- If the feature is too broad or mixes multiple deliverables, pick one strong slice that can stand alone while remaining materially aligned to the goal.\n- Use the platform and factory intent to prefer real shipped value over factory ceremony or preparatory work.\n- The finished issue should still make sense if someone later asks: 'If this issue ships cleanly, what real part of the goal is now done?'\n\nReturn JSON only with issue_title, issue_body, and issue_labels.\nDo not call gh directly.",
        "session_id": "goal-decomposer-${issue_number}"
      }
    },
    {
