        "shape": "diamond",
        "label": "Issue spec valid?"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "judge_issue",
      "kind": "llm_prompt",
      "title": "Judge issue quality",
      "dotAttributes": {
        "class": "issue_quality_judge",
        "benchmark_job_id": "goal.write_issue.judge",
        "llm_path_id": "capability.write_issue_item.judge_issue",
        "prompt_version": "2026-03-09.r1",
        "role_version": "1.0.0",
        "skill_id": "goal.write_issue.judge",
        "llm_model": "openai/gpt-5.3-codex",
        "label": "Judge issue quality",
        "output_format": "json",
        "outputs": "pass,decision,review_notes",
        "reasoning_effort": "low",
        "timeout": "${goal_decomposition_timeouts.issue_judge}",
        "prompt": "You are the issue quality judge for ${gh_repo}.\n\nJudge whether the created issue is aligned to the parent goal, grounded in current code reality, and executable as a single implementation issue on a shared wave branch.\n\nGoal issue JSON:\n${goal_issue}\n\nGoal context JSON:\n${goal_context}\n\nFeature JSON:\n${feature}\n\nCreated issue spec JSON:\n${issue_spec}\n\nCreated issue URL:\n${issue_url}\n\nUse read to load the issue content if needed. Evaluate:\n- Is the issue small enough for one builder-reviewer loop, but substantial enough to ship a real increment?\n- Does it depend on unstated exploration to discover basic files, boundaries, or intended behavior?\n- Do acceptance criteria describe what done looks like for this issue alone?\n- Does it stay aligned to the parent goal and avoid creating hidden follow-up work?\n\nReturn JSON with:\n{\n  \"pass\": true,\n  \"decision\": \"approved|revise\",\n  \"review_notes\": \"Actionable feedback. Empty when approved.\"\n}\n\nRules:\n- If pass=true, decision must be 'approved' and review_notes should be empty or a short confirmation.\n- If pass=false, decision must be 'revise' and review_notes must explain exactly what to change.\n- Keep review_notes concrete: cite missing files, boundaries, acceptance criteria, or scope problems.\n\nReturn JSON only."
      }
    },
